{
  "$mulmocast": {
    "version": "1.1"
  },
  "lang": "en",
  "title": "Three Talking Avatars",
  "description": "Reika, Seiya and Ken take turns, each with their own voice and talking avatar (loaded by URL from mulmocast-media). Needs the npm packages avatarscript and onnxruntime-node.",
  "avatarParams": {
    "position": {
      "y": "100%",
      "scale": "52%"
    }
  },
  "speechParams": {
    "speakers": {
      "Reika": {
        "provider": "openai",
        "voiceId": "nova",
        "displayName": {
          "en": "Reika"
        },
        "avatar": {
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/receptron/mulmocast-media/main/avatars/reika",
          "position": {
            "x": "16%"
          }
        }
      },
      "Seiya": {
        "provider": "openai",
        "voiceId": "echo",
        "displayName": {
          "en": "Seiya"
        },
        "avatar": {
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/receptron/mulmocast-media/main/avatars/seiya",
          "position": {
            "x": "50%"
          }
        }
      },
      "Ken": {
        "provider": "openai",
        "voiceId": "onyx",
        "displayName": {
          "en": "Ken"
        },
        "avatar": {
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/receptron/mulmocast-media/main/avatars/ken",
          "position": {
            "x": "84%",
            "scale": "36%"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "beats": [
    {
      "speaker": "Reika",
      "text": "Hey, you two. We've already started. Today we're introducing talking avatars, remember?",
      "image": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "markdown": [
          "# Three Talking Avatars",
          "",
          "Reika · Seiya · Ken"
        ]
      },
      "avatarParams": {
        "emotion": "angry",
        "motions": [
          {
            "motion": "nod",
            "at": "Today"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Seiya",
      "text": "Sorry, sorry. Hi everyone, I'm Seiya. Each of the three of us was made from a single illustration.",
      "image": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "markdown": [
          "# From a single picture",
          "",
          "- One illustration → a talking avatar",
          "- Blinks, mouth shapes, swaying hair"
        ]
      },
      "avatarParams": {
        "emotion": "happy",
        "motions": [
          {
            "motion": "nod",
            "at": "Hi everyone"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Ken",
      "text": "I'm Ken. Each of us has a different voice, too. You just give every speaker in the script a voice and an avatar.",
      "image": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "markdown": [
          "# One voice per speaker",
          "",
          "```json",
          "\"Ken\": {",
          "  \"voiceId\": \"onyx\",",
          "  \"avatar\": { \"source\": \"https://…/avatars/ken\" }",
          "}",
          "```"
        ]
      },
      "avatarParams": {
        "emotion": "relaxed"
      }
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Reika",
      "text": "So how do you match the mouth to the words? Don't tell me it just flaps open and shut at random.",
      "image": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "markdown": [
          "# What about the mouth?"
        ]
      },
      "avatarParams": {
        "emotion": "angry",
        "motions": [
          {
            "motion": "tilt",
            "at": "Don't tell me"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Seiya",
      "text": "It really does match. The speech is lined up against the text, and the mouth switches between its shapes as the sounds change.",
      "image": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "markdown": [
          "# Matched to the speech",
          "",
          "- Speech lined up against the text",
          "- Mouth shapes: a · i · o"
        ]
      },
      "avatarParams": {
        "emotion": "happy",
        "motions": [
          {
            "motion": "think",
            "at": "lined up"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Ken",
      "text": "Even when we're not talking, we stay on screen. We blink, and our hair sways a little.",
      "image": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "markdown": [
          "# Even when not talking",
          "",
          "- Stay on screen",
          "- Blinking, swaying hair"
        ]
      },
      "avatarParams": {
        "emotion": "neutral",
        "motions": [
          {
            "motion": "nod",
            "at": "We blink"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Reika",
      "text": "Hmm. Well, it's better than I expected. N-not that I'm impressed or anything.",
      "image": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "markdown": [
          "# …Not bad"
        ]
      },
      "avatarParams": {
        "emotion": "surprised",
        "motions": [
          {
            "motion": "surprise",
            "at": "better than"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Seiya",
      "text": "So stubborn. The avatars live in the avatars folder of the media repository, so please give them a try.",
      "image": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "markdown": [
          "# Try them",
          "",
          "`mulmocast-media/avatars/`",
          "",
          "ani · marilyn · reika · seiya · ken"
        ]
      },
      "avatarParams": {
        "emotion": "happy",
        "motions": [
          {
            "motion": "giggle",
            "at": "So stubborn"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Ken",
      "text": "That's all. See you in the next script.",
      "image": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "markdown": [
          "# See you"
        ]
      },
      "avatarParams": {
        "emotion": "relaxed",
        "motions": [
          {
            "motion": "nod",
            "at": "See you"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}